.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt NVMFT 4D
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nvmft
.Nd NVMe over Fabrics target port provider
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver is a port provider for the SCSI Target Mode Framework (STMF).
It lets NVMe over Fabrics hosts use STMF logical units as NVMe
namespaces over TCP.
.Pp
Each NVM subsystem is an STMF target port named by its subsystem NQN.
Subsystems are created and deleted with
.Xr nvmfadm 8 .
A logical unit is a namespace of every subsystem whose target port has
a view of it, and its namespace ID is the logical unit number of that
view plus one.
A host is known to STMF by its host NQN, so host groups made of host
NQNs control which hosts see which namespaces; see
.Xr stmfadm 8 .
.Pp
The driver does not listen on the network.
The
.Xr nvmfd 8
daemon accepts each connection and passes it to the driver once the
host has sent its Connect command.
.Pp
Hosts are not authenticated and connections are not encrypted.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa
.It Pa /kernel/drv/amd64/nvmft
Device driver (x86)
.It Pa /kernel/drv/nvmft.conf
Driver configuration file
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nvmfadm 8 ,
.Xr nvmfd 8 ,
.Xr sbdadm 8 ,
.Xr stmfadm 8
